#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1266 expect=violation domain=SE
#note "SEUPDES is not in the dataset at all while ETCD is UNPLAN -- the guarded variable's column is ABSENT ENTIRELY. Under EC-43 an absent column is all-missing, so empty(<var>) is TRUE on every row and the rule reports its defect on the rows its other conjuncts select. The variable was removed from Requirements.Variables.All on 2026-08-27 (owner ruling) because it is Permissible in this domain and NO rule anywhere reports its absence -- neither a specific presence rule nor the generic Required/Expected rules, which do not cover Permissible variables. Before that removal this scenario would have taken a silent dataset SKIP."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | SE | 01-701-1015 | 1 | UNPLAN | Unplanned Element
